-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ט/6: הבהרות בנוגע לחוזרנו תשס"ט/4
-- Clarifications of circular תשס"ט/4 (the agreement with the secondary
-- teachers' organisation on new bagrut bonuses in mathematics and English,
-- the telephone-expense refund, and pay for work with pupils with learning
-- disabilities): whom it covers, that the 2% per questionnaire replaces the
-- old addition from 1.9.2008, that the added weekly hours start only on
-- 1.9.2009, the maximum position, and the scope of the learning-disabilities
-- arrangement.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT daydate

§ `תשס"ט/6 הבהרות בנוגע לחוזרנו תשס"ט/4`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date (29.3.2009), addressee, greeting, subject line and the lead-in: following circular תשס"ט/4 on the collective agreement for pay for work with pupils with learning disabilities, and the many questions it raised, the clarifications below; no rule of its own.

-- Circular תשס"ט/4, which this one clarifies, is not imported (each circular
-- is encoded on its own words); what this circular takes from it is named as
-- an input below.

@desc The teachers' organisations a teaching employee may belong to, or none.
DECLARE `union affiliation` IS ONE OF
    `the Teachers' Union (Histadrut HaMorim)`
    `the Secondary Teachers' Organisation (Irgun HaMorim)`
    `unaffiliated`

@desc The two posts section 3's maximum position distinguishes.
DECLARE `post` IS ONE OF
    `a teacher`
    `a principal`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as this circular asks about him.
DECLARE `teaching employee` HAS
    `employed in post-primary education`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed in post-primary (על-יסודי) education, middle schools included where section 4 says so
    `paid by an owner`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc receives the salary from an owner of educational institutions (הבעלויות)
    `paid by the Ministry of Education`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc receives the salary from the Ministry of Education
    `works at an owner with salary merged in the civil service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc works at an owner but the salary is merged in the civil service under a loan agreement (איחוד משכורות)
    `affiliation`                              IS A `union affiliation`
    `post held`                                IS A `post`

DECLARE `clarification action` IS ONE OF
    `change the scope of the hours of a bagrut-preparation teacher`
    `employ beyond the maximum position` HAS `position employed` IS A NUMBER

§§ `1 סעיף 1ב – תחולת ההסכם`

-- Section 1, first paragraph: the agreement on new bagrut bonuses in
-- mathematics and English and the telephone-expense refund apply to every
-- teaching employee in post-primary education paid by an owner, whatever
-- the organisation he belongs to. The affiliation is not read at all.
@ref akn:art_1/p1
GIVEN e IS A `teaching employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bagrut and telephone agreement applies to` e IF
        e's `employed in post-primary education`
    AND e's `paid by an owner`

-- Section 1, second paragraph: the new bagrut bonuses (only they, not the
-- telephone refund) apply also where the employee works at an owner and the
-- salary is merged in the civil service under a loan agreement.
@ref akn:art_1/p2
GIVEN e IS A `teaching employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the new bagrut bonuses apply to` e IF
        `the bagrut and telephone agreement applies to` e
    OR (    e's `employed in post-primary education`
        AND e's `works at an owner with salary merged in the civil service`)

GIVEN e IS A `teaching employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the telephone refund applies to` e IF
    `the bagrut and telephone agreement applies to` e

§§ `2 סעיף ג(1א) – תוספת 2% לשאלון`

-- "The pay addition customary until the agreement was signed" and the 2%
-- addition itself are defined in circular תשס"ט/4 section ג(1)(א); here they
-- are inputs, per questionnaire.
@desc The additions a bagrut questionnaire may carry, as circular תשס"ט/4 section ג(1)(א) sets them.
DECLARE `questionnaire additions` HAS
    `the 2% addition`                    IS A NUMBER @desc the "2% per questionnaire" addition of circular תשס"ט/4 section ג(1)(א), shekels; an input of that circular
    `the addition customary before`      IS A NUMBER @desc the pay addition customary for the questionnaire until the agreement was signed, shekels; an input

`the 2% addition starts` MEANS Date 1 9 2008

-- Section 2: the 2% addition comes INSTEAD of the old addition, not on top
-- of it, and is computed from the start of school year תשס"ט, 1.9.2008.
@ref akn:art_2/p1 akn:art_2/p2
GIVEN q IS A `questionnaire additions`, `day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the questionnaire addition on` q `day` IS
    IF `day` AT LEAST `the 2% addition starts`
    THEN q's `the 2% addition`
    ELSE q's `the addition customary before`

§§ `3 סעיף ג(1ב) – תוספת שעות שבועיות`

`the added weekly hours start` MEANS Date 1 9 2009

-- Section 3, first paragraph: the added weekly hours for a teacher preparing
-- for the bagrut take effect only from 1.9.2009.
@ref akn:art_3/p1
GIVEN `day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the added weekly hours are in force on` `day` IF
    `day` AT LEAST `the added weekly hours start`

-- Section 3, second paragraph: in תשס"ט the teachers entitled to
-- bagrut-preparation bonuses in hours go on being employed as now, and the
-- scope of their hours is not changed. Time is counted in school months of
-- 2008/09 (common.l4: September = 1); the prohibition runs to the year's end.
@ref akn:art_3/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clarification action`
DECIDE `no change to bagrut-preparation hours in תשס"ט` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    SHANT `change the scope of the hours of a bagrut-preparation teacher`
    WITHIN `month number` August
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 3: in 2008/09 the hours of teachers entitled to bagrut-preparation bonuses are not changed"

-- Section 3, third paragraph: under the new agreement the added preparation
-- hours are an integral part of the employee's position in the year he
-- presents his pupils for the bagrut in those subjects.
@ref akn:art_3/p3
GIVEN `position without the added hours` IS A NUMBER,
      `added preparation hours as a share of a position` IS A NUMBER,
      `presents pupils for the bagrut this year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position with the added hours` `position without the added hours` `added preparation hours as a share of a position` `presents pupils for the bagrut this year` IS
    IF `presents pupils for the bagrut this year`
    THEN `position without the added hours` PLUS `added preparation hours as a share of a position`
    ELSE `position without the added hours`

-- Section 3, fourth paragraph: no teaching employee is employed beyond the
-- maximum position, printed "(150%/140% מורה/מנהל)". Which figure belongs to
-- which post the text does not settle (F-2008-09_tashsat_06-a): the corpus
-- text, in reading order, puts 150% first; the page, read right to left,
-- shows 140% first.
`the figures in the order the corpus text carries them` MEANS LIST 1.5, 1.4
`the figures in the order the page shows them, right to left` MEANS LIST 1.4, 1.5
`the posts in the order printed` MEANS LIST `a teacher`, `a principal`

GIVEN p IS A `post`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum position paired by the corpus text's order` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a teacher`   THEN 1.5
    WHEN `a principal` THEN 1.4

GIVEN p IS A `post`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum position paired by the page's order` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a teacher`   THEN 1.4
    WHEN `a principal` THEN 1.5

`the two orders pair the figures with the posts differently` MEANS
        (NOT (`the figures in the order the corpus text carries them`
              EQUALS `the figures in the order the page shows them, right to left`))
    AND (NOT (`the maximum position paired by the corpus text's order` `a teacher`
              EQUALS `the maximum position paired by the page's order` `a teacher`))
#ASSERT `the two orders pair the figures with the posts differently`

-- The reading adopted (F-2008-09_tashsat_06-a): the page as printed, read in
-- its own direction: a teacher 140%, a principal 150%.
@ref akn:art_3/p4
GIVEN p IS A `post`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum position` p IS
    `the maximum position paired by the page's order` p

GIVEN e IS A `teaching employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clarification action`
DECIDE `no employment beyond the maximum position` e IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    SHANT `employ beyond the maximum position` `position employed`
          PROVIDED `position employed` GREATER THAN `the maximum position` (e's `post held`)
    WITHIN `month number` August
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 3: no teaching employee is employed beyond the maximum position allowed"

§§ `4 סעיף 2 – הסדר לתגמול עובדי הוראה עבור עבודה עם תלמידים לקויי למידה`


-- Section 4, first paragraph: the arrangement covers every teaching employee
-- in post-primary education, middle schools included, paid by the Ministry
-- of Education and/or by an owner.
@ref akn:art_4/p1
GIVEN e IS A `teaching employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the learning-disabilities arrangement applies to` e IF
        e's `employed in post-primary education`
    AND (e's `paid by the Ministry of Education` OR e's `paid by an owner`)

-- Section 4, second paragraph: how the pay is carried out in schools that
-- moved to Ofek Hadash will be published separately. Nothing is decided for
-- them here, so for such a school the amount is an input.
@ref akn:art_4/p2
GIVEN `the school moved to Ofek Hadash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this circular decides the implementation for` `the school moved to Ofek Hadash` IF
    NOT `the school moved to Ofek Hadash`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

-- Worked examples. The shekel figures are round placeholders: the amounts
-- are circular תשס"ט/4's.
`a teacher at an owner, unaffiliated` MEANS
    `teaching employee` WITH
        `employed in post-primary education`  IS TRUE
        `paid by an owner`                    IS TRUE
        `paid by the Ministry of Education`   IS FALSE
        `works at an owner with salary merged in the civil service` IS FALSE
        `affiliation`                         IS `unaffiliated`
        `post held`                           IS `a teacher`

`a teacher at an owner with salary merged in the civil service` MEANS
    `teaching employee` WITH
        `employed in post-primary education`  IS TRUE
        `paid by an owner`                    IS FALSE
        `paid by the Ministry of Education`   IS FALSE
        `works at an owner with salary merged in the civil service` IS TRUE
        `affiliation`                         IS `the Teachers' Union (Histadrut HaMorim)`
        `post held`                           IS `a teacher`

`a middle-school teacher paid by the Ministry` MEANS
    `teaching employee` WITH
        `employed in post-primary education`  IS TRUE
        `paid by an owner`                    IS FALSE
        `paid by the Ministry of Education`   IS TRUE
        `works at an owner with salary merged in the civil service` IS FALSE
        `affiliation`                         IS `the Secondary Teachers' Organisation (Irgun HaMorim)`
        `post held`                           IS `a teacher`

#ASSERT `the bagrut and telephone agreement applies to` `a teacher at an owner, unaffiliated`
#ASSERT `the new bagrut bonuses apply to` `a teacher at an owner with salary merged in the civil service`
#ASSERT NOT `the telephone refund applies to` `a teacher at an owner with salary merged in the civil service`
#ASSERT NOT `the bagrut and telephone agreement applies to` `a middle-school teacher paid by the Ministry`
#ASSERT `the learning-disabilities arrangement applies to` `a middle-school teacher paid by the Ministry`

`a questionnaire` MEANS
    `questionnaire additions` WITH
        `the 2% addition`               IS 200
        `the addition customary before` IS 150

#ASSERT `the questionnaire addition on` `a questionnaire` (Date 1 9 2008) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the questionnaire addition on` `a questionnaire` (Date 31 8 2008) EQUALS 150
#ASSERT NOT `the added weekly hours are in force on` (Date 1 6 2009)
#ASSERT `the added weekly hours are in force on` (Date 1 9 2009)
#ASSERT `the position with the added hours` 1 0.1 TRUE EQUALS 1.1
#ASSERT `the maximum position` `a teacher` EQUALS 1.4

-- The maximum position, run on a timeline: employing the teacher at 120% is
-- no breach; employing him at 145% is.
#TRACE `no employment beyond the maximum position` `a teacher at an owner, unaffiliated` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `employ beyond the maximum position` 1.2 AT 1
#TRACE `no employment beyond the maximum position` `a teacher at an owner, unaffiliated` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `employ beyond the maximum position` 1.45 AT 1
#TRACE `no change to bagrut-preparation hours in תשס"ט` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `change the scope of the hours of a bagrut-preparation teacher` AT 3
